Step 5: Create styles.css
In the same folder as your index.qmd, create a brand new file and name it exactly styles.css. This is where you control all the visual design — colors, fonts, spacing, etc.
CSS works by targeting a class name and saying “anything with this class should look like this.” For example:
.hero {
  background-color: #F0EBE1;
  padding: 5rem 2rem;
  text-align: center;
}
That says: find anything with the class hero, give it a warm background color, lots of padding, and center the text. Every class name you used in your .qmd (like hero, project-card, section-card) needs a matching block in this file.
You build out the file by writing one block per class, defining things like background-color, border, border-radius (for rounded corners), padding (inner spacing), and font-size.
